  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Atmospheric CO2/C13 data from various Canadian locations, 1974-present",
  "description": "Atmospheric carbon dioxide measurements from Alert, NWT (1974- 2000 ,continuing), Sable Island (1974-1981), Cape St. James (1974-1981), Kains Island (1978-1984)and Quatsino Light Station (1981-1984). Also from ships of opportunity travelling between Canada and Japan (Canadian Ace, Canada Maru, Skaugran) and Canada and Australia (Lillooet) and oceanographic cruises.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: Monitoring long term changes of atmospheric carbon dioxide; 13C:12C ratios .\n\nSupplemental information: Risk Justification: Custodian will be leaving soon and has a large quantity of data not secured in a regional data centre. Risk of Loss: High Impact Justification: Long term time series (more than 10 years), large volume of high quality data Impact of Loss: High Recommended Action: Obtain access to the data and bring data to archives.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23570056",
